# app/lamad — the lamad pillar EPR app

Considered coverage, no edit-time gate: this app's recurring drifts are already
held by **structural gates in the lint/test chain**, which converge better than
edit-time prompts would —

- **SSR-entry contract** (`src/main.server.ts`): exports `default` bootstrap +
  `renderApplication` wrapper; `SSR_DOCUMENT` root tag matches the
  `app.component.ts` selector; no custom-element `…/register` side-effect
  imports in the server graph. Gated by `app/scripts/lint-ssr-entry.mjs`
  (in `pnpm run lint`) — the authoring-time twin of elohim-render's typed
  compose refusals. Scar tissue: the 2026-07-18 selector-mismatch regression
  that kept /lamad dark to crawlers for two weeks.
- **Minted links, never literals**: `app/scripts/lint-route-literals.mjs`
  (spec §7.1 epr-route-claims-link-conformance).
- **Declared route surface**: `src/app/generated/route-claims.ts` is codegen —
  never hand-edit generated files.
- **Cross-workspace imports**: this bundle's `tsconfig.json` maps `@app/<pillar>/*`
  at `app/elohim-app`'s private source tree, and elohim-app maps `@app/lamad/*`
  back — a live cycle, with the cross-pillar content substrate on this side of
  it. Gated by `app/scripts/lint-workspace-imports.mjs` (in `pnpm run lint`)
  against the declared debt in `app/scripts/workspace-import-baseline.json`:
  down-only, a new or deepened edge fails. Scar tissue: the extraction created a
  BUNDLE seam that then got read as a DOMAIN seam, and the arrow inverted to
  core → pillar one locally-reasonable import at a time, unobserved because
  nothing aggregated them. See `app/CLAUDE.md` §Bundle seams are not domain seams.

Dependencies must be declared in this app's own `package.json` — resolution via
another workspace app's hoist is drift (lived: `vite-tsconfig-paths`,
2026-07-18). Content-shaped; enforced by review until a validator-EPR exists.

The canonical EPR-app SSR pattern (the four declarative touches) is documented
in `app/CLAUDE.md`.
